From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: replenish the RX buffers reaped without a complete MSDU

Return descriptors to their owning refill rings even when the batch contains
no complete MSDU. Purge incomplete skbs rather than leaking them.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/ath12k/20261016124620.76-1-26rote@gmail.com/
Fixes: d889913205cf ("wifi: ath12k: driver for Qualcomm Wi-Fi 7 devices")
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_rx.c
@@ -786,9 +786,6 @@
 
 	spin_unlock_bh(&srng->lock);
 
-	if (!total_msdu_reaped)
-		goto exit;
-
 	for (device_id = 0; device_id < ATH12K_MAX_DEVICES; device_id++) {
 		if (!num_buffs_reaped[device_id])
 			continue;
@@ -799,6 +796,11 @@
 		ath12k_dp_rx_bufs_replenish(partner_dp, rx_ring,
 					    &rx_desc_used_list[device_id],
 					    num_buffs_reaped[device_id]);
+	}
+
+	if (!total_msdu_reaped) {
+		__skb_queue_purge(&msdu_list);
+		goto exit;
 	}
 
 	ath12k_wifi7_dp_rx_process_received_packets(dp, napi, &msdu_list,
